-- The licence this gateway enforces on `data/s2-tci-512.tif`: full resolution
-- only inside a licensed area, coarse imagery everywhere.
--
-- One CQL2 expression, evaluated once per region. Each branch guards on
-- `region.kind` or `region.overview_level` first, because a region carries
-- only the properties its kind has and an unresolved operand denies.

-- The structure. `header`, `ghost_area`, `ifd`, `tile_offsets`,
-- `tile_byte_counts`, `geo_keys` and `tag_values` are the only names the COG
-- resolver emits, and without them no reader can find a tile at all --
-- `tile_offsets` most of all, since it is the array `sparse::plan` edits.
region.kind = 'metadata'

-- Every overview, at every level. This is the shape of a real imagery licence
-- -- browse resolution for everyone, full resolution for subscribers -- and it
-- is also what makes the AOI recoverable: the coarse levels still show, at
-- 20 m and worse, the ground the full-resolution rule withholds. That trade is
-- the licensor's to make and it is stated rather than hidden.
--
-- `> 0` and not `>= 1` for the same reason `overview_level` is a rank and not a
-- ratio: level 0 is full resolution, and a higher level is always coarser.
OR region.overview_level > 0

-- Full resolution, inside the licensed area only.
--
-- `S_CONTAINS(<area>, region.geom)` and NOT `S_INTERSECTS(region.geom, <area>)`.
-- The difference is the whole rule. A tile is the unit of service, so an
-- existential predicate grants a tile on *any* contact with the area and its
-- pixels outside the licence go out with it. Measured on this exact polygon --
-- the union of tiles x 5-9, y 5-9, edges lying on tile boundaries --
-- `S_INTERSECTS` grants 49 tiles where `S_CONTAINS` grants 25, and four of the
-- extra 24 touch the area along a single edge with zero interior overlap.
--
-- `S_CONTAINS` errs the other way: an area smaller than one tile grants
-- nothing. For a licence that is the correct direction to be wrong in, and it
-- is why the polygon is snapped to tile boundaries rather than drawn inside
-- them -- a hand-drawn AOI will under-serve at the edges, which is a licensing
-- conversation and not a leak.
--
-- The polygon is EPSG:32610 metres, the CRS the file's GeoKeys declare and
-- therefore the CRS `region.geom` is in. cql2's spatial operators are planar
-- and CRS-agnostic (issue #5), so a polygon in degrees would match nothing and
-- deny everything -- fail-closed, but for the wrong reason.
OR (region.overview_level = 0 AND S_CONTAINS(POLYGON((
     525580 4148800, 551180 4148800, 551180 4174400, 525580 4174400, 525580 4148800)),
   region.geom))
